{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CQuantumObservableUniverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CQuantumObservableUniverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.state_sections_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.state_sections_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L90-L90","doc":"`Γ_c(M, S)` is trivial: all compactly supported state sections are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.compactStateSections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.compactStateSections","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L88-L88","doc":"The type of compactly supported sections of the state bundle `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_cohomology_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.adjoint_cohomology_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L86-L86","doc":"`H⁰(M, Ad(P))` is trivial: all global adjoint sections are equal.\nIn a vector space this means `H⁰(M, Ad(P)) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.adjointSections","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.adjointSections","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The type of global sections of the adjoint bundle `Ad(P)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.toCRManifoldData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse.toCRManifoldData","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L81-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CQuantumObservableUniverse","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L77-L90","doc":"**ℂ quantum observable universe**: CR manifold data satisfying the\nvanishing conditions `H⁰(M, Ad(P)) = 0` and `Γ_c(M, S) = 0`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:c-quantum-observable-universe}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:c-quantum-observable-universe","label":"ex:c-quantum-observable-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.reeb_preserves_contact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.reeb_preserves_contact","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L75-L75","doc":"The Reeb field preserves the contact form: θ(ξ(p)) = θ(p) for all p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.reebField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.reebField","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The Reeb vector field `ξ`, characterised by `ι_ξ dθ = 0` and `θ(ξ) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.contact_nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.contact_nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The contact form is non-degenerate: there exists a point where θ ≠ 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.contactForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.contactForm","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The contact form `θ` as a real-valued function on `M`.\n\nWas `M → R_q`. A contact form is a real 1-form: this structure's own\n`reebField` docstring characterises `ξ` by `ι_ξ dθ = 0` and `θ(ξ) = 1`,\nand neither the exterior derivative nor the normalisation `= 1` means\nanything over `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. §7c reserves `ℝ` for archimedean\nconstructs and this is one; the library copy always had `ℝ`\n(bean `qou-u87j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.rs_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.rs_sum","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.s","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.r","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Levi form signature `(r, s)` with `r + s = n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.n_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.n_pos","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L56-L56","doc":"`n ≥ 1`, as the docstring above already claimed. Taken from the library\ncopy, which had it where this one did not (bean `qou-u87j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.n","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L53-L53","doc":"CR dimension `n ≥ 1`; real dimension of `M` is `2n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.topM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.topM","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.M","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The underlying smooth manifold carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CRManifoldData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CRManifoldData","kind":"structure","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L41-L75","doc":"**CR manifold data** for the ℂ realisation (local prerequisite).\n\nRe-declared from the sibling block `c-quantum-universe.lean`\n(`def:c-quantum-universe`) so this sibling is a self-contained\ncompilation unit — importing the library `CRRealisation` module\nwould collide with its own `CQuantumObservableUniverse`\ndeclaration.  Keep field-for-field in sync with the sibling. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:c-quantum-universe","label":"ex:c-quantum-universe","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-universe.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/c-quantum-observable-universe.lean#L36-L39","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nMirrors the sibling block `c-quantum-universe.lean`; see\n`QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}